From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orders Team <orders-team@example.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:48:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(debug): keep replay snapshots of recent responses

Support keeps asking "what exactly did the API return to this customer?",
and the access log only records the status and the latency. Record a
snapshot of every response, keyed by the trace id that already appears in
each log line and in Tempo, and serve it from GET /debug/replay/{trace_id}.

Snapshots are fixed-size records (REPLAY_BUFFER_BYTES, 256 KiB) so the
replay tool can read them at fixed offsets; that fits a full
GET /orders?limit=100 page.

Release 1.2.0.
